# Smoke

> **Prefix** `SMOKE-` · **Reset** none · **Cost** ~10 min

The fast "is this build even drivable" pass over {{scope}}/{{kebabCase name}}.
Green ⇒ go on to the suites that matter for what changed; red ⇒ stop and fix,
because everything after this reads on top of it.

The boxes are deliberately about the **shell** rather than the feature: a route
that renders, a locale that resolves, a control a keyboard can reach, a console
with nothing in it. Replace them as the service grows real surfaces — and move
any box a spec takes over into
[`../reference/automation.md`](../reference/automation.md).

## Preconditions

The dev server up on :{{port}} per [`../setup.md`](../setup.md), devtools open,
a 1440×900 viewport.

> **Agent note**: wait on the route's own heading, never on a timeout — the app
> renders `home.title` only once i18n has initialized, so a heading assertion is
> the earliest honest ready signal.

## Boxes

- [ ] `SMOKE-1` · **Open `/` with the console open** → the heading and the
  tagline render; no console message at `warn` or `error` level.
- [ ] `SMOKE-2` · **Reload the page** → the route re-renders from the URL alone;
  no flash of an empty shell, no error boundary.
- [ ] `SMOKE-3` · **Press the counting button three times** → the live region
  reads the new count each time, and announces it (`aria-live="polite"`), rather
  than only repainting.
- [ ] `SMOKE-4` · **Switch the app to each locale it ships** → every visible
  string changes with it; no key leaks through as its raw dotted path, and no
  sentence stays English.
- [ ] `SMOKE-5` · **Reach the button with Tab alone, then activate it with Enter
  and with Space** → focus is visible at every stop, the order matches the
  reading order, and both keys activate it.
- [ ] `SMOKE-6` · **Open a route the app does not define** → a real not-found
  renders inside the shell; no white screen, no unhandled rejection in the
  console.
